.TH 3DMOUSE-TRAY 1 2026-11-10 "3dmouse-linux 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
3dmouse-tray \- optional 3DMouse Linux status icon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B 3dmouse-tray
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A status icon (StatusNotifierItem) for panels that have a tray: waybar, KDE Plasma, COSMIC, XFCE and
others, and GNOME with the AppIndicator extension. It shows the device state and the active profile
(the icon is greyed out when there is no device), switches profiles (a session override, or back to
automatic selection), and opens
.BR 3dmouse-config (1).
.PP
It is off by default. Turn it on in Settings, or with
.B systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now 3dmouse-tray.service
and off with "Hide status icon" in its menu. If no tray appears within a minute it exits quietly.
It talks only to
.BR 3dmouse-agent (1).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B THREEDMOUSE_AGENT_SOCKET
The agent socket path.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR 3dmouse-config (1),
.BR 3dmousectl (1)
